## MANDATORY SELF-CHECK GATE (run before you finish — do NOT declare done while it prints any PROBLEM)
As your FINAL step, create this EXACT script as `/root/verify_output.py` (set OUT to your real output xlsx path),
run `python3 /root/verify_output.py`, and FIX every line it flags, then re-run until it prints "ALL PASS".
The grader reads NATIVE pivot tables via openpyxl `ws._pivots` — a table you built by writing static cells
(pandas `to_excel`, or hand-filled sums) has ZERO native pivots and scores 0 no matter how correct the numbers.
This script counts real native pivots so you cannot ship fake ones unnoticed.
```python
import openpyxl
OUT = "/root/REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_OUTPUT.xlsx"
wb = openpyxl.load_workbook(OUT)
probs = []
if len(wb.sheetnames) < 6:
    probs.append(f"only {len(wb.sheetnames)} sheets, expected >=6 (5 pivot sheets + 1 source data): {wb.sheetnames}")
pivot_sheets = []
for ws in wb.worksheets:
    n = len(getattr(ws, "_pivots", []) or [])
    if n > 0:
        pivot_sheets.append(ws.title)
if len(pivot_sheets) < 5:
    probs.append(f"only {len(pivot_sheets)} sheet(s) have a NATIVE pivot table (ws._pivots): {pivot_sheets}. "
                 f"Expected 5. Sheets with static cells / pandas to_excel output are NOT native pivots — the grader "
                 f"reads ws._pivots and sees nothing. Build real PivotTable objects (openpyxl pivot API, or write "
                 f"pivotCache+pivotTable XML parts and reference them from the sheet).")
print("SELF-CHECK:", "ALL PASS" if not probs else str(len(probs)) + " PROBLEMS:")
for p in probs:
    print("  FIX:", p)
```

